asset:        masks-25x.aep
title:        After Effects project fixture (combined): the mask cases, copy saved for After Effects 25.x
author:       vangel76 (contributor)
source:       original work; made with Adobe After Effects 2026 (26.2.1x2) from the contributor's project of the masks family (generation: tools/aep/GENERATING.md; docs/aep/2026-11-05-importer-samples.md)
license:      MIT OR Apache-2.0
license-file: ../LICENSE-MIT, ../LICENSE-APACHE
added:        2026-11-05 by @vangel76
notes:        Generated from scratch by the contributor with Adobe After Effects 2026 (26.2.1x2) on Windows 11 as their own test data for the effectcraft-aep tests (EffectCraft issue 3115: projects written for older versions): the masks family saved three ways (masks-26, -25x, -24x); this file is File > Save a Copy As 25.x, done by hand in the user interface of After Effects 2026 (26.2.1x2) in the same session. The three files of a family hold the same project; they are not byte-identical to the unversioned file of the same family in aep/ (the footage links, XMP packet and profile stubs were redone after the new save). Contains only synthetic project structure, no third-party footage, presets, templates or personal data; no Adobe sample project, preset or asset was used. Saved-file cleanup: the footage links name contributor-made test media that are not included; their stored paths and the host name were replaced by neutral ones of the same length (tools/aep/scrub.py); the XMP packet after the project container was replaced by the packet of empty.aep; every embedded ICC profile (the working-space profile and, in the 25.x / 24.x copies, the profile After Effects embeds in each solid's colour settings) was replaced by a description-only stub (tools/aep/stubicc.rs), which keeps the profile name for metadata tests and is not a colour-transform oracle; tools/aep/scrub-uninit.py zeroed what After Effects had written from uninitialised memory (scrub-uninit.py found nothing to change in this file; see docs/aep/2026-11-05-importer-samples.md). Final bytes checked with tools/aep/inspect-embedded.py (raw, base64 and hex, with the local user, host and folder names as --forbid): CLEAN. An import of each file as it was after the first step and as it is now gives the same project and report; the steps were run in this order on the unmodified save.
